  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">‍<a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-an-epoch-2\"><strong id=\"\">Epochs</strong></a> as part of the current <a id=\"\" href=\"http://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-radixs-babylon-mainnet\"><strong id=\"\">Babylon</strong></a> version of the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Public Network</strong></a><strong id=\"\"> </strong>are targeted to last 5 minutes. The number of \"<a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-rounds-and-what-does-rounds-per-second-mean\"><strong id=\"\">rounds</strong></a>\" within an epoch is adjusted dynamically by the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-the-radix-protocol\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Protocol</strong></a> in order to achieve this There is a hard-coded minimum of 500 rounds, and a maximum number of 3000 rounds in an epoch. See the <a id=\"\" href=\"http://docs.radixdlt.com\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Tech Docs</strong></a> for more.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-an-epoch\"><strong id=\"\">What’s an epoch?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-do-xrd-emissions-work\"><strong id=\"\">How do XRD emissions work?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-xrd-staking-emissions-rewards-penalties-are-calculated-general\"><strong id=\"\">How XRD staking emissions rewards are calculated - general</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-rounds-and-what-does-rounds-per-second-mean\"><strong id=\"\">What are “rounds” and what does “rounds per second” mean?</strong></a></li></ul><p id=\"\"><br></p>",
